From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:50:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Route layout construction through the flat tree (shadow
 content renders)

Box construction now reads children through Node::flat_children()
(hosts hoist their shadow root's children; everything else unchanged):
the push_* collectors, flow classification, flex/grid text checks, the
inline-layout builders, and the emptiness early-out - which would
otherwise skip construction entirely for a host whose only content is
its shadow tree. Take-based iteration gets flat macro/method variants
(iter_flat_children[_and_pseudos]!, iter_flat_children[_and_pseudos_]
mut) with host-mixed sourcing: ::before/::after belong to the host
while children come from its shadow root; the light variants stay for
callers that want DOM semantics.

Damage propagation gets the same hop: shadow trees live outside
`children`, so without it a shadow mutation after first paint never
bubbles CONSTRUCT damage to the host and new content never renders.

With the style traversal already flat (previous patch), unslotted
light children are now consistently invisible: never styled, never
laid out - per spec for slotless shadow trees.

This removes the last users of the iter_children /
iter_children_and_pseudos macros, so they go too.
